+
+## FAQ & Rulings
+
+**Foreign Invasion and unrest:** Cole Wehrle clarified on April 30, 2023 that unrest does **not** add to a Foreign Invasion's primary attack strength or determine its resulting tower levels. Use the ordinary die roll for both attack strength and halving to create towers; the event still uses the Company-defense procedure and its secondary unrest attacks. Do not apply the normal primary Crisis's added unrest to this special event. [Designer ruling](https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/2962161/article/42192767#42192767). The rules already avoid closing Foreign Invasion orders twice: Region Loss's additional closure is only for an Invasion Crisis.
+
+**Applicable official errata:** The publisher links the [official errata discussion](https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/2936700/official-errata), whose original designer post links the full internal correction list. The assigned Second Printing rulebook incorporates the core procedural corrections, including forced prize-piece reuse, empty Court, deployment boundaries, Region Loss and Elephant priority. Corrected setup cards supply Bengal's 1758 control token and 1813 control/share-value tokens. Printed card corrections also specify: Mercantile/Diplomatic Connection reducing a check to zero dice means failure; Company Fraud is played at start of Revenue, rolls one die per officeholder and takes twice the highest roll from Balance to a minimum of zero; Public Demands Impeachment returns member to supply and office card to vacancies; Military Oversight's demoted Commander is eligible as an officer for reappointment. These are card-specific effects, not changes to the normal check/hiring procedures.
 
